{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122679","id":4328178879,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAfrEvw","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122679","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122679.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122679.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122679","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122679/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122679/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122679/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/fbfa59ad28f8ed1874716e63b8d4b69a2621dc95","number":122679,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Update editor recursion detection to function for scenes","user":{"login":"kaseda1027","id":51314433,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzE0NDMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51314433?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaseda1027","html_url":"https://github.com/kaseda1027","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaseda1027/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaseda1027/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaseda1027/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaseda1027/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaseda1027/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaseda1027/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaseda1027/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaseda1027/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaseda1027/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #104769\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nAI was not used in any way during this development. All code was authored completely by me.\r\n\r\nThis change enhances the existing resource recursion detection in the editor. Previously, the recursion detection would only run if the object being updated was itself a `Resource` - meaning no recursion detection was happening when updating properties on nodes. This allows that recursion detection to occur for nodes, and allows them to detect if the scene they are in is referenced recursively. Attempts to assign a resource a value that would create a cyclic dependency will be rejected with an error message. The error message now also includes the path of the resource that was detected in the recursion.\r\n\r\nAdmittedly, this differs somewhat from the discussion on the issue itself, particularly in the segment of code that I've updated. While the issue was focused on updating the code responsible for writing `PackedScene` files, this update prioritizes detecting and rejecting them in the editor.\r\n\r\nThe recursion detection references the `PackedScene` files that are _on disk_ at the time, meaning it's possible to make a cyclic reference between two scenes, then save each independently, and create a cyclic dependency without prompting the warning message. This would be solved by adding or moving this detection to the code that writes `PackedScene` files. This pull request will catch the issue earlier, but has potential to miss this edge case (though should work the majority of the time) - a fix in the writer would catch them always, but not until the scene is saved. It could be worth implementing both.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, I'm questioning my use of the scene path to track the root scene. It was the easiest option available - but perhaps there's a more proper solution. I'd happily accept feedback from more experienced contributors. I'm also sorry if it's bad practice to submit code for a team that the original 